  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Run Umbraco Automate automations from the palette, plus safety and legibility work on the palette itself.\n\n- Umbraco Automate automations can be started from anywhere in the backoffice. An automation appears only if its author gave it a Manual or Scheduled trigger, and only if you can already access it - Automate re-checks that when it fires. Type > to search automations only, or a bare > to list them.\n- Every automation confirms before it runs and shows what it will do first: its workspace, step count, and whether it sends email, publishes content or reaches an external service. Anything irreversible asks you to type the automation's name; if the palette cannot work out what an automation does, it asks for the typed name rather than assuming it is harmless.\n- Nothing changes if you do not have Automate installed - no empty state, no requests, and > is ordinary search text.\n- A confirmation can no longer be pressed through by double-tapping Enter, Enter does nothing while a search is still running, and holding Enter or Escape down no longer repeats.\n- Confirmations now have Cancel and Run buttons, and each kind of result has its own icon instead of one shared generic shape.\n\nNo new C# and no new endpoint: the integration talks to Automate's own Management API as the signed-in user. Full changelog: https://github.com/BMichal93/Umbraco.Community.CommandPalette/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
